    "description": "This course introduces data structures and algorithms with emphasis on non-linear structures, including hash tables, trees, and graphs. Students learn representation, operations, and algorithms for searching, traversing, and optimizing these structures. Through problem-solving and implementation, the course develops analytical skills for designing efficient algorithms applicable to real-world computing, networking, and data-intensive applications."
